<title>USA: Metropolitan Financial Q1 net, share rise.</title>
<headline>Metropolitan Financial Q1 net, share rise.</headline>
<dateline>MAYFIELD HEIGHTS, Ohio 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>Three months ended March 31,</p>
<p>							1997	     1996</p>
<p> Net Interest Income			   $6,438	  $4,685</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses			585	     307</p>
<p> Net interest income after provision	5,853	   4,378</p>
<p> Noninterest income				 926	     922</p>
<p> Noninterest expense			    4,867	   4,133</p>
<p> Income before federal income taxes	 1,912	   1,167</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes		     701	     451</p>
<p> Net Income					 1,211	     716</p>
<p>Per Share Data (A):</p>
<p>   Net income					0.34	    0.23</p>
<p>   Book value					8.73	    8.27</p>
<p>   Tangible book value			   7.78	    7.20</p>
<p>   Stock Price				    11.00	     N/A</p>
<p>Performance ratios:</p>
<p>   Return on average assets		   0.61%	   0.46%</p>
<p>   Return on average equity		   15.87	   11.16</p>
<p>   Interest rate spread			  3.21	    3.03</p>
<p>   Net interest margin			   3.47	    3.26</p>
<p>Average interest-earning assets to</p>
<p>average interest-bearing liabilities</p>
<p>						     105.02	  104.30</p>
<p>   Noninterest expense to average assets   2.47	    2.67</p>
<p>   Efficiency ratio			     65.98	   72.73</p>
<p>NOTES: (A) -- Common shares outstanding at March 31, 1997 and 1996 were 3,525,635 and 3,125,635, respectively.  Average common shares outstanding in 1997 and 1996 were 3,525,635 and 3,125,635, respectively.</p>
<p>Full company name is Metropolitan Financial Corp.</p>
